==== Opening the case ====

**Note:** This will void your warranty!
**WARNING:** When the case is open, parts carrying live (110/230V) current are accessible. You must unplug the AP before opening! Do not plug the AP in while open!  

To open the case, remove the sticker at the back of the device with the default login setting.
Remove the screw that was below the sticker.
Pry open the lid from the backside of the device with a prying tool starting from one of the air outlets at the top or bottom of the device.

